{"book":23,"chapter":33,"context":{"chapter":33,"title":"The King in His Beauty","summary":"A woe on a treacherous destroyer turns into a prayer for help, and the question is asked who can live with God's consuming fire. Zion will see the King in His beauty and become a quiet, secure home where sins are forgiven.","background":"The treacherous 'spoiler' (vv. 1, 8) fits Sennacherib, who took Hezekiah's tribute and still attacked Jerusalem (2 Kings 18:13-17). Verse 18 recalls the siege, when foreign officials counted towers and collected tribute. Jerusalem had no great river, so in verse 21 the Lord Himself becomes its broad river, where no enemy warship can sail.","customs":[{"term":"Who shall dwell with the devouring fire?","verses":"33:14-16","note":"Echoes the questions asked of worshipers entering the temple: who may stand in God's presence? (Psalm 15; 24:3-4)."}],"watchFor":["'Thine eyes shall see the king in his beauty' (v. 17).","A tent whose stakes will never be pulled up (v. 20).","The Lord is judge, lawgiver and king (v. 22)."],"connections":["Psalms 15:1-5","Psalms 24:3-4","2 Kings 18:13-17","Psalms 46:4"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["הוֹי","ho","H1945","HTj","woe to!"],["שׁוֹדֵד","shoded","H7703","HVqrmsa","[the] destroyer"],["וְאַתָּה","ve'atah","H859","HC/Pp2ms","and you"],["לֹא","lo'","H3808","HTn","not"],["שָׁדוּד","shadud","H7703","HVqsmsa","[have been] destroyed"],["וּבוֹגֵד","uvoged","H898","HC/Vqrmsa","and [the] traitor"],["וְלֹא","velo'-","H3808","HC/Tn","and not"],["בָגְדוּ","vagedu","H898","HVqp3cp","people have dealt treacherously"],["בוֹ","vo","H9033","HR/Sp3ms","with him"],["כַּהֲתִמְךָ","kahatimkha","H8552","HR/Vhcc/Sp2ms","when finishing you"],["שׁוֹדֵד","shoded","H7703","HVqrmsa","destroying"],["תּוּשַּׁד","tushad","H7703","HVHi2ms","you will be destroyed"],["כַּנְּלֹתְךָ","kanelotekha","H5239","HR/Vhcc/Sp2ms","when completing you"],["לִבְגֹּד","livgod","H898","HR/Vqcc","to deal treacherously"],["יִבְגְּדוּ","yivgedu-","H898","HVqi3mp","people 